  "body": {
    "source_format": "markdown",
    "plain_text": "The Euclidean algorithm gives 252 = 1*198 + 54, 198 = 3*54 + 36, 54 = 1*36 + 18, 36 = 2*18. So gcd(252,198)=18. Reverse the chain: 18 = 54 - 36 = 54 - (198 - 3*54) = 4*54 - 198 = 4*(252 - 198) - 198 = 4*252 - 5*198.",
    "markdown": "The Euclidean algorithm gives $252 = 198 + 54$, $198 = 3\\cdot54 + 36$, and $54 = 36 + 18$. So $\\gcd(252,198)=18$. Reverse the chain: $18 = 54 - 36 = 54 - (198 - 3\\cdot54) = 4\\cdot54 - 198 = 4(252 - 198) - 198 = 4\\cdot252 - 5\\cdot198$."
  },
